# Part of Cloudberry's greenplum_schedule (src/test/regress), as the port
# runs it on a coordinator and three segments: the tests of the schedule
# that bear on M2 -- dispatch, distribution, Motions, joins, aggregates,
# subqueries, partitions, DML -- on M5's append-optimized and
# column-oriented tables and external tables, on M6's resource queues and
# groups, and on M7's materialized views, in the schedule's order.
#
#   run   the test runs here, in both passes -- or in the one pass named
#         after it, the rest of the line saying what the other meets;
#         cloudberry/ holds a difference reviewed and kept, where one pass
#         has one
#   skip  it needs what the port does not have yet: the rest of the line is
#         the first of Cloudberry's statements it refuses, as the port says
#   port  a test of the port's own, sql/ and expected/ here, run where the
#         line is: what a skipped test would have left for the tests after it,
#         or a setting the schedule gives the tests of a group
#   group the tests after it, to the next such line, are a group: each group
#         has a cluster of its own, test_setup and gp_setup first, and the
#         groups of a pass run side by side, each in the schedule's order.
#         A group whose name begins "mirrors" has Cloudberry's demo cluster
#         whole: a mirror for each segment, and a standby coordinator.  One
#         whose name begins "tcp" has its nodes reach one another over TCP.
#         The groups are cut by time, the ORCA pass's, and a test that reads
#         what another made is in its group (bb_mpph's tables,
#         bb_memory_quota's).  namespace_gp has one of its own, ns, in the
#         schedule's place, whose comparison of pg_namespace across the
#         nodes must come before any test's temporary schema: a node makes
#         its own, pg_temp_N by its own backend's number, with an OID of its
#         own, where Cloudberry's coordinator dispatches one name and OID for
#         a session's.
#
# Every test of the schedule is listed.  The ones the port had left for M7 --
# fault injection, FTS, the interconnect's settings, and the rest -- come
# last, in the schedule's order, tried on 2026-09-26: those that run are in
# groups of their own, m7a and m7b, and each that is skipped says what
# stopped it.  "differs:" says it for a test that stops at nothing, and
# answers otherwise than Cloudberry's expected output says.
#
# One test of Cloudberry's parallel_schedule runs here too, ivm, its
# incremental views on a cluster: Cloudberry runs that schedule on its
# cluster before this one.
